    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This study developed an algorithm based on Simulated Annealing to constrain the permeability and porosity distributions of a given reservoir model to the well test data collected at several wells. The technique can be used for single or multiple well tests. In order to keep the execution time of this algorithm within an acceptable range, the perturbation on the pressure transient due to a local heterogeneity is approximated by an analytic influence function. The results given by this approximation were compared to the results given by a simulator, and found to be reliable. The algorithm was tested on several examples, showing that the use of the analytic influence function allows considerable reduction in the computing time. Moreover, it was shown that such a constraining leads to a better prediction of a waterflood performed during a longer period of time.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
